{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444396-v5-lets-speculate-about-tokyo","id":1444396,"title":"V5 lets speculate about Tokyo!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-17T16:11:35-07:00","id":1444396,"title":"V5 lets speculate about Tokyo!","content":"In the Camarilla book we get a little sneak peak at Tokyo. It gives us some tasty things to look at in terms of what is going on there. Help me speculate on some possibilities behind these mysteries!<br /> <br /> 1. Standing in crowds appears to quell the beast<br /> - Mechanically I am thinking of doing something like &quot;As long as the PC is standing in a very crowded area, treat his hunger as one less&quot;<br /> I am wondering what causes this effect. Maybe a sleeping elder with some sort of effect on the city. I want to speculate that this has to do with what is said later about vampires in Tokyo seeming abnormally detached and vacant<br /> <br /> 2. Strong camarilla presence but very cut off due to high levels of technology and the second inquisition<br /> - of course we also have strike force zero here. obviously any v5 version should be a lot less gonzo. No mention of the kue jin which is probably fine. In my games ill probably just treat the eastern courts as a separate but still vampiric sect like the Ashirra. <br /> <br /> 3. Social hierarchy based on age<br /> - isnt this just regular vampiric society?<br /> <br /> 4. Vampires upon reaching 300 all leave for Kyoto except for one old nosferatu<br /> - I have a hard time seeing vampires all just relinquishing power and heading off to another town. Maybe this is a soylent green thing and the beckoning is just feeding them all to some elder. Maybe there is some sort of curse<br /> <br /> 5. Mayumi Shibusaki the Tzimisce Autarkis is the most powerful vampire in town and doesn't hate tremere.<br /> - a quick google check tells me that Mayumi is a 12th gen. Seems pretty weak to be the most powerful vampire in charge. Also if the camarilla is strong there, where is the prince? Now arguably, Tokyo is too big to be ruled by a single prince and so may Mayumi is a playing a lot of smaller regional princes off each other.<br /> <br /> 6. All the vampires seems detached and vacant <br /> - this makes me think something is going on with the beast. Maybe a golconda quest gone wrong has started to spread like a virus or something else.<br /> <br /> <br /> Give me your speculations and ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T16:28:11-07:00","id":1444400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am wondering what causes this effect. Maybe a sleeping elder with some sort of effect on the city. I want to speculate that this has to do with what is said later about vampires in Tokyo seeming abnormally detached and vacant </div> </div> </div>I figure this could be a Ley Line effect. It seems designed to preserve the Masquerade by preventing vampires from ever frenzying in a place that would have hundreds of witnesses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - I have a hard time seeing vampires all just relinquishing power and heading off to another town. Maybe this is a soylent green thing and the beckoning is just feeding them all to some elder. Maybe there is some sort of curse </div> </div> </div>It might be a Beckoning like situation or a direct threat that if you don't go there, that you are destroyed by the Methuselahs living there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - a quick google check tells me that Mayumi is a 12th gen. Seems pretty weak to be the most powerful vampire in charge. Also if the camarilla is strong there, where is the prince? Now arguably, Tokyo is too big to be ruled by a single prince and so may Mayumi is a playing a lot of smaller regional princes off each other. </div> </div> </div>I think she is the Prince, she just doesn't call herself such. Sort of like Queen Anne Bowesley. The fact that all the Elders go to Kyoto means her job is just to be the lord over the Ancilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-